# Server data layer

Page components orchestrate UI; **data fetching lives in `src/lib/`**.

## Structure

| Layer | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| `src/app/**/page.tsx` | Parse params/searchParams, call lib loaders, render |
| `src/lib/**/get-*.ts`, `load-*.ts` | Drizzle queries, mapping, shared `Promise.all` batches |
| `src/app/**/actions/*.ts` | Mutations + `revalidatePath` |

```tsx
// ❌ Inline Drizzle in a page
export default async function ImportDetailPage({ params }) {
  const rows = await db.select().from(transactions).where(...);
}

// ✅ Page calls a lib helper
const detail = await getImportDetail(id);
```

## Dedupe before copy-pasting

If two routes need the same `Promise.all([...])` block, extract one loader (e.g. `loadMonthReportData()`). Reuse mappers like `toCategoryOptions()` instead of inline `.map(({ id, name, color, icon }) => ...)`.

## Fewer DB round-trips

- Reuse counts already returned by a paginated query when they answer the same question (e.g. unfiltered total when no filters are active).
- Do not add a second `count()` query “just in case” — check whether the first query's `totalCount` is sufficient.
- Batch independent reads with `Promise.all`; don't serialize queries that don't depend on each other.

Behavior must stay the same: only skip a query when the remaining data **provably** covers the use case (empty-database vs filtered-empty are different).
